   169	function Annexes({ addr }: { addr: Address }) {
   170	  const [copied, setCopied] = useState<'' | 'ok' | 'fail'>('');
   171	  const curl = `curl -s -X POST https://api.hyperliquid-testnet.xyz/info -H 'content-type: application/json' -d '{"type":"userFills","user":"${addr}"}'`;
   172	  return <section className="annexes">
   173	    <article className="annex-doc" id="judges">
   174	      <p className="fig1-n">Annex B</p><h2>For judges: how to verify it on-chain</h2>
   175	      <ol className="steps">
   176	        <li><p><b>The contract exists and holds the terms.</b> Open <a href={`${EXPLORER}/address/${addr}`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" className="fig">{short(addr)}</a> on the HyperEVM testnet explorer. The source is in the project repo at <span className="fig">contracts/src/Pledge.sol</span>, and the explorer's <a href={`${EXPLORER}/address/${addr}`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">contract page</a> shows the deployed bytecode; it has no owner, no admin and no withdraw before the end date.</p></li>
   177	        <li><p><b>It cannot be cancelled.</b> Press the three "Simulate" buttons in <a href="#c4" onClick={e => { e.preventDefault(); document.getElementById('c4')?.scrollIntoView(); }}>clause 4</a>. Each one asks the live contract. While the term runs, each comes back "Rejected by the contract". After the end date the team's withdrawal is allowed, as the terms say. "Could not check (network)" means the RPC failed, not the contract. {addr.toLowerCase() === DEMO.toLowerCase() ? ' On this demo agreement the same calls were also sent as real transactions and reverted; the links are next to each check.' : ''}</p></li>
   178	        <li><p><b>Check this agreement's fills on HyperCore.</b> They are also listed in <a href="#c6" onClick={e => { e.preventDefault(); document.getElementById('c6')?.scrollIntoView(); }}>clause 6</a>, read from the same API. Run this and look for side "A" (sell) fills. An agreement that has not sold yet returns an empty list.</p><pre className="code fig">{curl}</pre><button className="btn-outline" onClick={() => (navigator.clipboard ? navigator.clipboard.writeText(curl) : Promise.reject()).then(() => setCopied('ok'), () => setCopied('fail'))}>{copied === 'ok' ? 'Copied' : 'Copy command'}</button>{copied === 'fail' && <p className="bad">The browser blocked copying. Select the command above and copy it by hand.</p>}</li>
   179	        <li><p><b>The full flow works from a wallet.</b> On a separate test agreement, our click-through test drafted a new agreement, deposited 0.5 HYPE, triggered a sale and reconciled it, from a browser wallet on testnet: agreement <a href={`${EXPLORER}/address/${E2E.pledge}`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" className="fig">{short(E2E.pledge)}</a>, create <a href={`${EXPLORER}/tx/${E2E.create}`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" className="fig">{short(E2E.create)}</a>, sale <a href={`${EXPLORER}/tx/${E2E.sale}`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" className="fig">{short(E2E.sale)}</a>, reconcile <a href={`${EXPLORER}/tx/${E2E.reconcile}`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" className="fig">{short(E2E.reconcile)}</a>. The fill was 0.5 HYPE at 22.538 against bids already on the testnet book.</p></li>
   180	      </ol>
   181	      <h3 className="rail-h3">What is real and what is simulated</h3><ul className="rvl"><li><span className="rv-b"><Badge variant="outline">real, testnet</Badge></span><span>Contract deployed, terms fixed, cancel and early withdraw revert</span></li><li><span className="rv-b"><Badge variant="outline">real, testnet</Badge></span><span>Deposit of HYPE from HyperCore into the contract</span></li><li><span className="rv-b"><Badge variant="outline">real, testnet</Badge></span><span>Sale as an IOC order on the HyperCore HYPE/USDC book, filled size counted against the daily cap</span></li><li><span className="rv-b"><Badge variant="outline">real, testnet</Badge> (an earlier IOC was cancelled and refunded)</span><span>Unfilled orders return their size to the day's allowance</span></li><li><span className="rv-b"><Badge variant="outline">real, testnet</Badge></span><span>Sale blocked under the floor, sale blocked before the start date, team withdraws the remainder after the end date, anyone (not just the team) can trigger a sale. Txs in the repo: deployments/feature-tests.json and keeper-test.json</span></li><li><span className="rv-b"><Badge variant="outline">fork-simulated</Badge> see Annex A</span><span>The daily allowance resetting across several days, and a price crash below the floor mid-term</span></li><li><span className="rv-b"><Badge variant="outline">planned</Badge></span><span>The 0.25% fee, mainnet, other tokens</span></li></ul>
   182	    </article>
   183	    <article className="annex-doc" id="business">
   184	      <p className="fig1-n">Annex C</p><h2>Business model</h2>
   185	      <p><b>Who pays:</b> the token team or foundation that locks supply. They get a public, checkable promise about how the locked supply will be sold, which they can show to exchanges, market makers and holders. Buyers and keepers pay no PLEDGE fee, only normal network gas.</p>
   186	      <p><b>Fee (proposed, not in the testnet contract):</b> 0.25% of filled sale proceeds, taken in USDC as each sale fills. A team only pays when the plan is working. For comparison, Streamflow charges 0.16 SOL per contract plus 0.19% of the tokens vested, or 0.16 SOL plus 0.5% for a token lock, both on the allocated amount; Sablier's interface charges $0.99 per stream withdrawal. PLEDGE's proposed fee is on filled sale proceeds instead.</p>
   187	      <p><b>Market:</b> Tokenomist counts <span className="fig">$97.43B</span> of tokens unlocked in 2025, of which <span className="fig">$18.77B</span> went to insiders (team and investors), the supply holders worry about most. HYPE itself unlocked about <span className="fig">$496M</span> in 2025. Illustration only: if 1% of insider unlocks were sold through PLEDGE at 0.25%, that is about <span className="fig">$470K</span> a year in fees. This is the global unlock market, not evidence of demand on Hyperliquid or of willingness to pay.</p>
   188	      <p className="meta">Sources: <a href="https://www.tokenomist.ai/research/2025-token-unlocks-review-a-complete-breakdown-of-emissions-insider-vesting-and-market-impact" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Tokenomist 2025 Token Unlocks Review</a>; <a href="https://streamflow.finance/blog/how-much-does-streamflow-cost" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Streamflow pricing</a>; <a href="https://docs.sablier.com/concepts/fees" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Sablier fees</a>.</p>
   189	    </article>
   190	  </section>;
